From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:53:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] windows.globalization: add Language's statics, IsWellFormed
 and the input method's language.

Word asks the Language factory for ILanguageStatics, which it did not
have.  tools/languageprobe measured Windows 11:

- IsWellFormed follows BCP 47's grammar, grandfathered tags taken
  whole, case not minded, with two things of Windows' own: a language
  subtag of four to eight letters is turned away, and a singleton that
  begins an extension twice is not well formed, where a variant twice
  is.  NULL is not well formed, and not an error.
- CurrentInputMethodLanguageTag is the language of the thread's
  keyboard layout, written as a language tag, which for Chinese has the
  script: zh-Hans-CN where the locale is zh-CN.

ILanguageStatics2's TrySetInputMethodLanguageTag switches the thread to
an installed keyboard layout of the language, and says no for one that
has none.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 8e5778b166c7c3dd49cecb8146a4435e22d23117)

